s10-9-p5 : Block
s10-9-p5 = prose (cons "**One symbolic debugging operation.** Let \(\mathsf{Run}(F)\) be an execution family for a particular program under its specified environment and machine semantics, and let \(o:\mathsf{Run}(F)\to O\) record the observed event prefix. For a recorded prefix \(y:O\), the debugger's input is the dependent type" (cons "\[" (cons "\mathsf{CompatibleRun}(y):=\sum_{\rho:\mathsf{Run}(F)}(o(\rho)=y)." (cons "\tag{10.23}" (cons "\]" (cons "If a new authenticated event \(e\) arrives, its observation-update operation \(u_e:O\to O'\) and extended observation \(o':\mathsf{Run}(F)\to O'\) define a restriction" (cons "\[" (cons "\mathsf{CompatibleRun}'(y,e):=" (cons " \sum_{(\rho,p):\mathsf{CompatibleRun}(y)}(o'(\rho)=u_e(y))." (cons "\tag{10.24}" (cons "\]" (cons "A residual evaluator maps this family to the still-possible ledger values or causal predecessors; it does not invent the missing packets. When a packet is recovered, the new equality witness narrows the fiber, and cached symbolic results are reused only under their recorded observation dependencies. Navigating from source to machine instructions uses the compiler's established trace relation; enlarging the cut to include a network handler uses the handler interpretation defined in §7.6. Thus an actual interactive operation has typed inputs, an observation update, and a defined output family." nil))))))))))))
